       The function ffoorrmm__uusseerrppttrr returns a pointer (which may  be  NNUULLLL).   It
       does not set eerrrrnnoo.

       The function sseett__ffoorrmm__uusseerrppttrr returns EE__OOKK (success).

PPOORRTTAABBIILLIITTYY
       These  routines emulate the System V forms library.  They were not sup‐
       ported on Version 7 or BSD versions.

       The user pointer is a void pointer.  We chose not to leave it as a char
       pointer for SVr4 compatibility.

